  "question": {
    "text": "The domain of the function $f(x)=\\sqrt{x-\\sqrt{1-x^2}}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gOFHW",
      "text": "$\\left[-1,-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right] \\cup\\left[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}, 1\\right]$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "oay3C",
      "text": "$[-1,1]$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GBFUQ",
      "text": "$\\left(-\\infty,-\\frac{1}{2}\\right] \\cup\\left[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},+\\infty\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "oGFwG",
      "text": "$\\left[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}, 1\\right]$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For $f(x)$ to be defined, we must have<br />$x-\\sqrt{1-x^2} \\geq 0 \\text { or } x \\geq \\sqrt{1-x^2}>0 \\text { or } x^2 \\geq 1-x^2$<br />or $x^2 \\geq \\frac{1}{2}$.<br />Now, $x^2 \\geq \\frac{1}{2} \\Rightarrow\\left(x-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)\\left(x+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\geq 0$<br />$\\Rightarrow x \\leq-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\quad \\text { or } \\quad x \\geq \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$<br />Also, $1-x^2 \\geq 0$ or $x^2 \\leq 1$.<br />Also, $x^2 \\leq 1 \\Rightarrow(x-1)(x+1) \\leq 0 \\Rightarrow-1 \\leq x \\leq 1$<br />Thus, $x>0, x^2 \\geq \\frac{1}{2}$ and $x^2 \\leq 1 \\Rightarrow x \\in\\left[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}, 1\\right]$",
    "image": null
  },
